  howpublished = {\url{https://www.infoblox.com/blog/threat-intelligence/scams-slaves-and-malware-as-a-service-tracking-a-trojan-to-cambodias-scam-centers/}},
  note         = {Published 10 April 2026. DNS-telemetry-led analysis of an Android banking trojan distributed as a service, assessed as operated at least in part from the K99 Triumph City compound, Sihanoukville. Approximately 35 new lure domains registered per month; 400 lure domains registered in 2025 analysed; targeting observed in at least 21 countries. Attack chain: VoIP impersonation of officials, migration to a messaging application, delivery of a link or QR code to a lure page, coached installation of a malicious APK, SMS one-time-passcode interception, and a counterfeit KYC overlay inducing the victim to perform facial recognition that authenticates the operator into the victim's banking application. Corroborated by testimony and material from individuals rescued from the compound}
}

